", "reference": "1897, H[erbert] G[eorge] Wells, chapter 18, in The Invisible Man: A Grotesque Romance, New York, N.Y.; London: Harper & Brothers Publishers, →OCLC:"}, {"text": "He herded them into a small and evil toilet and then through a window.", "reference": "1958, Graham Greene, Our Man in Havana, Penguin, published 1979, Part Four, Chapter 1, p. 125:"}, {"text": "Everyone in the tiny, crowded, hot, and evil-smelling kitchen […] has been invited to participate in a moment of history.", "reference": "1993, Carol Shields, chapter 1, in The Stone Diaries, Toronto: Random House of Canada, page 39:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "Producing or threatening sorrow, distress, injury, or calamity; unpropitious; calamitous.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "The owl shrieked at thy birth,—an evil sign;", "reference": "c. 1591–1592 (date written), William Shakespeare, “The Third Part of Henry the Sixt, […]”, in Mr. William Shakespeares Comedies, Histories, & Tragedies […] (First Folio), London: […] Isaac Iaggard, and Ed[ward] Blount, published 1623, →OCLC, [Act V, scene vi]:"}, {"text": "[…] he hath brought up an evil name upon a virgin of Israel:", "reference": "1611, The Holy Bible, […] (King James Version), London: […] Robert Barker, […], →OCLC, Deuteronomy 22:19:"}, {"text": "A little stay will bring some notice hither,\nFor evil news rides post, while good news baits.", "reference": "1671, John Milton, “Samson Agonistes, […].”, in Paradise Regain’d. A Poem. In IV Books. To which is Added, Samson Agonistes, London: […] J[ohn] M[acock] for John Starkey […], →OCLC, page 89, lines 438-439:"}, {"text": "“[…] with bandits and robbers roving over the land in these evil times of famine and war, how can it be said that this one or that stole anything? Hunger makes thief of any man.”", "reference": "1931, Pearl S. Buck, chapter 15, in The Good Earth, New York: Modern Library, published 1944, page 122:"}, {"text": "I cannot overestimate how much it meant to me to have the support of my brothers in BWMT/MACT both in and out of prison while I was laid up with pneumocystis pneumonia during those dog days of August 1987. My wall is decked with cards, letters, and pictures from those evil days, and my support system included rides, flowers, candy, magazines of every description, and lots of hugs from gay and lesbian brothers and sisters.", "reference": "1988 February 14, Richard Tremblay, “A Boat With A Sail”, in Gay Community News, volume 15, number 30, page 5:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(obsolete) Having harmful qualities; not good; worthless or deleterious.", "tags": ["obsolete"], "examples": ["an evil beast; an evil plant; an evil crop"], "quotes": [{"text": "A good tree cannot bring forth evil fruit.", "reference": "1611, The Holy Bible, […] (King James Version), London: […] Robert Barker, […], →OCLC, Matthew 7:18:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(computing, programming, slang) Undesirable; harmful; bad practice.", "tags": ["slang"], "examples": ["Global variables are evil; storing processing context in object member variables allows those objects to be reused in a much more flexible way."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": ["nefarious", "malicious", "malevolent", "wicked", "abandoned", "arrant", "bad", "bad apple", "bad seed", "baleful", "scurrilous", "baneful", "base", "black-hearted", "dark", "deleterious", "demonic", "depraved", "despicable", "detrimental", "devilish", "diabolical", "evil", "evil-minded", "facinorous", "flagitious", "harmful", "heinous", "ill-intentioned", "ill-natured", "immoral", "incorrigible", "iniquitous", "iniquous", "injurious", "knavish", "malefic", "maleficent", "malign", "malignant", "naughty", "niddering", "nidering", "niding", "nithing", "no-good", "peccaminous", "pernicious", "reprehensible", "reprobate", "satanic", "scathful", "sinful", "sinister", "sordid", "sullen", "ungodly", "unholy", "vicious", "vile", "villainous", "wrong"], "antonyms": ["good", "angelic", "benign", "good-minded", "just", "moral", "righteous", "well-intentioned"]}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "noun", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈiːvəl/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "[ˈɪi̯vəl] ~ [ˈɪi̯vl̩]", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈiːvɪl/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "[ˈɪi̯vɪl]", "tags": ["obsolete"]}], "forms": [{"word": "evils", "tags": ["plural"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "Moral badness; wickedness; malevolence; the forces or behaviors that are the opposite or enemy of good.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": ["The evils of society include murder and theft.", "Evil lacks spirituality, hence its need for mind control."], "quotes": [{"text": "The heart of the sons of men is full of evil.", "reference": "1611, The Holy Bible, […] (King James Version), London: […] Robert Barker, […], →OCLC, Ecclesiastes 9:3:"}, {"text": "The preposterous altruism too![…]Resist not evil. It is an insane immolation of self—as bad intrinsically as fakirs stabbing themselves or anchorites warping their spines in caves scarcely large enough for a fair-sized dog.", "reference": "1918, W[illiam] B[abington] Maxwell, chapter XVI, in The Mirror and the Lamp, Indianapolis, Ind.: The Bobbs-Merrill Company, →OCLC:"}, {"text": "IS ANYTHING more obvious than the presence of evil in the universe? Its nagging, prehensile tentacles project into every level of human existence. We may debate the origin of evil, but only a victim of superficial optimism would debate its reality. Evil is stark, grim, and colossally real.", "reference": "1963, Martin Luther King, Jr., “The Death of Evil upon the Seashore”, in Strength to Love, New York: Pocket Books, published 1964, →OCLC, page 71:"}], "synonyms": ["enormity"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "ar", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "شَرّ"}, {"language": {"code": "hy", "name": "Armenian"}, "word": "չարություն"}, {"language": {"code": "hy", "name": "Armenian"}, "word": "չարիք"}, {"language": {"code": "az", "name": "Azerbaijani"}, "word": "şər"}, {"language": {"code": "be", "name": "Belarusian"}, "word": "зло"}, {"language": {"code": "be", "name": "Belarusian"}, "word": "лі́ха"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "зло"}, {"language": {"code": "my", "name": "Burmese"}, "word": "အကုသိုလ်"}, {"language": {"code": "my", "name": "Burmese"}, "word": "မကောင်းမှု"}, {"language": {"code": "ca", "name": "Catalan"}, "word": "mal"}, {"language": {"code": "ceb", "name": "Cebuano"}, "word": "demonyo"}, {"language": {"code": "cmn", "name": "Chinese Mandarin"}, "word": "邪惡 /邪恶"}, {"language": {"code": "cmn", "name": "Chinese Mandarin"}, "word": "惡 /恶"}, {"language": {"code": "cs", "name": "Czech"}, "word": "zlo"}, {"language": {"code": "dlm", "name": "Dalmatian"}, "word": "mul"}, {"language": {"code": "da", "name": "Danish"}, "word": "ond"}, {"language": {"code": "da", "name": "Danish"}, "word": "ondskab"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "kwade"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "kwaad"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "slechte"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "euvel"}, {"language": {"code": "dz", "name": "Dzongkha"}, "word": "མ་རུངས་པ"}, {"language": {"code": "egy", "name": "Egyptian"}, "word": "Dw-w-t:nDs"}, {"language": {"code": "eo", "name": "Esperanto"}, "word": "malbono"}, {"language": {"code": "et", "name": "Estonian"}, "word": "kurjus"}, {"language": {"code": "et", "name": "Estonian"}, "word": "pahe"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "paha"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "pahuus"}, {"language": {"code": "fr", "name": "French"}, "wor